win32u, winemac.drv: Share opt-in software window surfaces across processes.

WebView2 paints into a child whose top-level window belongs to its host. The
Mac driver has no X11-style foreign drawable, so software GDI drawing had no
backing surface. Add an opt-in section-backed buffer and notify the owning
window after foreign drawing completes. Its native presentation stays with
the host. Keep the ordinary path unchanged without WINE_CROSS_PROCESS_GDI=1.

The shared recursive drawing lock is acquired before local surface locks;
notifications are asynchronous. Surface generations reject stale updates
following resize or destruction. Preserve CoreGraphics provider lifetime
with a separate presentation buffer. Bump the driver interface version so
an old driver cannot allocate a shorter window_surface structure.

